# checkin - WeCom (企业微信) hook token
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.hook_token` and replace the placeholder below:
#     cp .hook_token.example .hook_token        (Windows: copy .hook_token.example .hook_token)
#
# `.hook_token` is git-ignored. Never commit the real value, never paste it into
# an issue, a log or a README - in documentation it is always written as
# <WECOM_HOOK_TOKEN>.
#
# The token is sent as the `X-Hook-Token` request header (not in the URL), so it
# does not leak into access logs.
#
# Precedence: the CHECKIN_WEBHOOK_TOKEN environment variable wins over this file.
#     setx CHECKIN_WEBHOOK_TOKEN <WECOM_HOOK_TOKEN>
#
# Rules for this file:
#   * lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored
#   * the first remaining line is used as the token, verbatim
#   * rotating the token needs no restart and no code change: edit this file
#     (or the environment variable) and the next run picks it up
#   * if the token is wrong or unset, the notification is still delivered as a
#     local Windows popup instead of being dropped silently
#
# Replace the next line with the real token, then save:
<WECOM_HOOK_TOKEN>
